			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">This is what I don't understand about Dark Elves, they are so quick to kill their own children as babies.  Even gnolls know enough to wait until the pups are big enough to fight then send the weak ones out against the enemy prove themselves (and almost always die) freeing the pack from the weakness of the unfit young and maybe taking a few enemy with them.
<br />

<br />
So, for all their bragadocio, Tier'Dal seem to be less intelligent than gnolls, at least the truly evil ones do.
<br />

<br />
Kaldarye, let your child grow and thrive, let Greon become fond of his heir, if it truly is his, those of us who know him do wonder about that, and wait to see what the future brings.  You may have the heir to three or four great houses (or do you know about the other house Greon is heir to?) sucking at your breast.  According to a quick review of Tier'Dal legal code, murdered/sacrificed babies do not engender any inheritance rights, they have to at least last long enough to be dedicated to the temple, attain their rebirthing rights, and kill their first lightskin to become citizens and make you his (or her) heir.  
<br />

<br />
Wait until they are young, full of life and vigor and hate, and the apple of Greon's eye.  Something he can claim as his and endow as heir.
<br />

<br />
Then make his permakilling as painful and wretched as possible, preferably so Greon can watch his heir's last moments.  As the mother, you would then be able to claim inheritence to all the property of the decedent, and toss Greon's life into shambles at the same time.
<br />

<br />
Of course, if it isn't Greon's proceed with the soon as its born sacrifice, you don't want evidence of your infidelity to survive long enough for Greon to claim violation of the marriage contract and claim your life, your dowry, and all your property as penalty.  Why is it only the men who get this right in Tier'Dal society.  You would think the women would want equal rights dealing with proven infidelity, but wait, the traditional rape of the defeated lightskin women practiced by so many Tier'Dal men might make that too powerful a clause.  This raises another question, if half Tier'Dal children are so horrid a thing they must be sacrificed immediately at the temple, why the standard practice of raping the lightskin women, which stands a really good chance of creating them?  
<br />

<br />
But hey, if they were happy at home they wouldn't feel the need to frolic elsewhere.  
<br />

<br />
You Tier'Dal have some really harsh laws.  I'm really curious about the required vivisection (sans pain relief of any kind, physical or magical) of adulterers on unhallowed ground clause.  Is that ever really enforced?  I'm guessing one of your early lawmakers was seriously cuckolded, any ideas on that?<div style="vertical-align: bottom"><br /><br /><br />_________________<br />Micheall, Ranger, Tradeskiller, Hack Author</div></span><span class="gensmall"></span></td>
